Drop the spurious std_logic_vector() cast in qk_score_bram's BRAM read process.

score_io_type elements are `signed` (types_pkg.vhd:48), so converting the
signed source to std_logic_vector before assigning to a signed target is a
type error. Removing the cast makes the file analyze and elaborate cleanly
(verified with GHDL 4.1.0, --std=08).

Apply from the package root:
    patch -p1 -d rtl_excluded < patches/qk_score_bram-drop-slv-cast.patch
then move rtl_excluded/qk_score_bram.vhd into rtl/mirage/ and uncomment the
matching line in tcl/synth_utilization.tcl.

--- a/qk_score_bram.vhd
+++ b/qk_score_bram.vhd
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
     process (addr_off_0, bram_score)
     begin
         for i in 0 to TOK_CONTEXT * NUM_HEADS - 1 loop
-            bram_data_out(i) <= std_logic_vector(bram_score(addr_off_0 + i));
+            bram_data_out(i) <= bram_score(addr_off_0 + i);
         end loop;
     end process;
 
